      "math_academy_id": "e-14369",
      "problem": "If $a_{n+1}=2a_n-3$ with $a_1=4,$ then find the value of $a_2.$",
      "worked_solution": "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\na_{n+1}=2a_n - 3\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1={\\color{blue}4}.$\n\nWe compute $a_2$ by substituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1} & =2{a}_{n}-3 \\\\ {a}_{1+1} & =2{a}_{1}-3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2{a}_{1}-3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2(4)-3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a_2=5.$",
